WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.600
[The D Dorm]

3
00:02.600 --> 00:05.400
Honestly, I miss you every day.

4
00:05.420 --> 00:07.910
I long for you.

5
00:07.930 --> 00:12.550
Dreaming of you every single night.

6
00:13.110 --> 00:15.000
My shining moon.

7
00:15.020 --> 00:16.329
My everlasting love.

8
00:16.350 --> 00:17.960
I cannot stand it.

9
00:17.980 --> 00:20.460
I miss you, Gaysorn.

10
00:21.940 --> 00:22.970
Grandpa,

11
00:22.990 --> 00:24.090
what's wrong with you, huh?

12
00:24.330 --> 00:25.440
Well, I am disappointed!

13
00:26.180 --> 00:27.820
I thought Dew's grandmother

14
00:27.840 --> 00:30.470
was Gaysorn, the one I missed dearly,

15
00:30.490 --> 00:32.400
but she is not.

16
00:33.290 --> 00:34.580
My heart

17
00:34.600 --> 00:36.800
is shattered.

18
00:37.920 --> 00:40.210
Sadhu. I hope Grandpa's soul

19
00:40.230 --> 00:41.880
shatters, just as he said.

20
00:41.910 --> 00:42.640
Sadhu!

21
00:42.660 --> 00:43.980
How dare you curse me like that?!

22
00:44.380 --> 00:44.780
Huh?!

23
00:44.800 --> 00:46.500
Grandpa, he's the first person we asked.

24
00:46.520 --> 00:47.480
Why are you so down?

25
00:48.040 --> 00:49.960
"The first person"? What does that mean?

26
00:52.560 --> 00:54.190
It was "the first time," Auntie Duang.

27
00:54.740 --> 00:56.570
It's my first time eating at your restaurant.

28
00:56.600 --> 00:58.240
I usually just order food to eat in my room.

29
00:58.650 --> 01:00.120
Come more often, then.

30
01:00.220 --> 01:01.760
Your grandpa used to come here a lot.

31
01:01.860 --> 01:04.230
Before he died, he said he'd lower my rent.

32
01:04.680 --> 01:05.680
Lower your rent?

33
01:05.700 --> 01:07.060
When did I say that, huh?!

34
01:07.080 --> 01:08.280
Anus Duang!

35
01:09.100 --> 01:09.690
Oh, is that so?

36
01:10.120 --> 01:12.620
But is "Anus Duang" your full name?

37
01:13.850 --> 01:14.380
Look.

38
01:14.400 --> 01:15.310
[Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

39
01:15.330 --> 01:16.210
"Duangjai."

40
01:16.410 --> 01:17.130
Wait,

41
01:17.150 --> 01:19.150
Gramps only calls me "Anus Duang."

42
01:19.170 --> 01:19.910
How did you know that?

43
01:20.850 --> 01:22.289
Oh, it was just a guess.

44
01:22.310 --> 01:24.600
You look like you've got pain in your anus.

45
01:24.970 --> 01:25.690
No!

46
01:25.710 --> 01:26.710
I'm all good now.

47
01:26.730 --> 01:28.110
- Oh, you are?! - Yes!

48
01:28.130 --> 01:28.870
Oh, that's good news.

49
01:28.890 --> 01:30.330
But I'm not asking you to keep his promise.

50
01:30.350 --> 01:32.750
I just want to fulfill his wishes

51
01:32.770 --> 01:34.130
so he can rest in peace.

52
01:34.150 --> 01:35.860
- I see... Is that so? - Mm.

53
01:35.890 --> 01:36.970
Hey, Mom.

54
01:37.390 --> 01:39.640
You may be my mom, but if you're committing fraud,

55
01:39.789 --> 01:40.789
I'll arrest you.

56
01:40.810 --> 01:42.600
What fraud?!

57
01:42.620 --> 01:44.640
I was just teasing Dobby!

58
01:45.509 --> 01:46.860
Oh, teasing, huh?

59
01:48.500 --> 01:50.560
So, can you think of any tenants

60
01:50.580 --> 01:52.630
who have a relative named Gaysorn?

61
01:52.650 --> 01:53.930
Danis,

62
01:53.950 --> 01:55.840
"Auntie Duang" isn't the Civil Registration Office, you know.

63
01:55.860 --> 01:57.020
I don't know everything.

64
01:57.039 --> 01:58.600
I only know a little. - I see.

65
01:58.640 --> 02:00.720
I only know who they are, where they come from,

66
02:00.740 --> 02:02.930
their partner's name, what they do for a living, how much they make,

67
02:02.950 --> 02:04.480
and what they like to eat. That's it.

68
02:04.500 --> 02:05.930
Wow, you only know a little, huh?

69
02:05.950 --> 02:06.950
If you knew any more than this...

70
02:06.970 --> 02:08.520
would you even know what brand of underwear they wear?

71
02:08.539 --> 02:10.139
- I do know that about some. - Huh?!

72
02:11.290 --> 02:15.620
♫You only one, just you, the only one♫

73
02:15.640 --> 02:20.320
♫Millions around, no one's like you, baby♫

74
02:20.340 --> 02:21.360
Singing it wrong, too.

75
02:22.260 --> 02:23.590
♫Dance a little, black shirt♫

76
02:23.610 --> 02:24.920
♫Dance a little, black shirt♫

77
02:24.940 --> 02:26.130
- Hey! - Ugh!

78
02:26.150 --> 02:27.070
You're messing with him.

79
02:27.090 --> 02:28.280
Do you even know him? He's a cop.

80
02:28.300 --> 02:29.190
- Oh, a cop? - Mm.

81
02:29.210 --> 02:30.060
Hello.

82
02:30.079 --> 02:30.960
Uh, hello...

83
02:31.079 --> 02:32.170
Hey, you.

84
02:32.190 --> 02:33.910
What kind of weird role are you playing this time?

85
02:34.000 --> 02:35.590
You can't call me that.

86
02:35.610 --> 02:36.610
You have to call me

87
02:36.980 --> 02:38.670
"Daisy."

88
02:39.610 --> 02:40.500
"Daisy"?

89
02:40.520 --> 02:41.900
- Daisy. - Daisy...

90
02:41.930 --> 02:42.750
- Mama. - Don't call me "you" again.

91
02:42.770 --> 02:43.930
- Yes, I'm sorry. - Don't do it again.

92
02:43.950 --> 02:45.910
Oh, I want to sit down now. I'm gonna sit down.

93
02:45.930 --> 02:46.810
Daisy?

94
02:46.829 --> 02:47.310
Hey,

95
02:47.329 --> 02:48.190
not like that.

96
02:48.320 --> 02:49.750
Say "Daisy."

97
02:50.150 --> 02:51.630
- Daisy? - Daisy.

98
02:51.650 --> 02:53.170
- Daisy. - Daisy.

99
02:53.190 --> 02:54.350
- Daisy. Dai... - Daisy. Dai...

100
02:54.370 --> 02:55.660
- sy. - Ugh!

101
02:55.870 --> 02:56.870
I know you're Daisy.

102
02:56.890 --> 02:57.950
That isn't important right now.

103
02:58.130 --> 02:58.980
Why did you drag your suitcase here?

104
02:59.000 --> 02:59.710
Oh,

105
02:59.730 --> 03:00.830
I'm staying with you tonight.

106
03:00.850 --> 03:01.620
Huh?

107
03:01.640 --> 03:03.310
I have an acting class with someone in your dorm.

108
03:03.680 --> 03:04.100
Who?

109
03:04.290 --> 03:04.920
Not telling you.

110
03:05.550 --> 03:07.580
Help! Help! A thief!

111
03:07.600 --> 03:08.360
- Hey. - Hey.

112
03:08.430 --> 03:09.430
Isn't that Dolly?

113
03:09.520 --> 03:10.750
Yes. Dollar, go!

114
03:10.830 --> 03:11.490
Dolly!

115
03:11.510 --> 03:12.120
Dolly!

116
03:13.500 --> 03:16.810
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

117
03:17.140 --> 03:20.840
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

118
03:23.310 --> 03:28.810
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

119
03:30.590 --> 03:35.290
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

120
03:37.710 --> 03:43.850
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

121
03:44.820 --> 03:49.390
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

122
03:49.410 --> 03:52.920
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

123
03:52.940 --> 03:56.520
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

124
03:56.540 --> 04:00.060
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

125
04:00.080 --> 04:02.720
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

126
04:02.740 --> 04:09.060
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

127
04:09.500 --> 04:16.170
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

128
04:16.649 --> 04:23.800
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

129
04:23.820 --> 04:30.740
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

130
04:30.760 --> 04:34.880
[The D Dorm]

131
04:35.200 --> 04:36.290
Dolly, are you alright?

132
04:36.320 --> 04:36.990
Dolly?

133
04:37.010 --> 04:38.810
- Are you hurt? - I'm fine, I'm fine.

134
04:38.830 --> 04:39.590
Go!

135
04:39.610 --> 04:41.300
- Oh, no, no, no. - Whoa, whoa.

136
04:50.960 --> 04:54.080
[Dome, occupation: police officer/drag queen]

137
04:54.100 --> 04:55.330
Oh, Teach!

138
04:55.659 --> 04:56.230
Huh?!

139
04:56.980 --> 04:57.890
They're my

140
04:57.920 --> 04:59.420
acting teacher.

141
04:59.440 --> 05:00.170
Huh?!

142
05:00.300 --> 05:02.670
By the way, you're so cool, Teach.

143
05:02.690 --> 05:03.770
Catching a thief like that.

144
05:06.140 --> 05:07.180
See?

145
05:07.310 --> 05:08.310
We're lucky

146
05:08.340 --> 05:09.490
Lieutenant Dome was there.

147
05:09.510 --> 05:10.230
Huh?!

148
05:10.250 --> 05:11.930
Dollar, who are you calling Lieutenant Dome?

149
05:11.990 --> 05:13.160
I'm off duty,

150
05:13.180 --> 05:14.960
so call me Queen Dominiga.

151
05:14.980 --> 05:15.840
Huh?!

152
05:15.860 --> 05:17.110
What is up with you?

153
05:17.130 --> 05:18.760
You kept saying, "Huh?!"

154
05:19.240 --> 05:21.090
I can't process this anymore.

155
05:21.220 --> 05:22.670
Everything is so confusing.

156
05:23.230 --> 05:24.590
Either way, thank you very much.

157
05:24.710 --> 05:26.550
If it weren't for you, I'd be in real trouble.

158
05:26.570 --> 05:27.420
Hey,

159
05:27.520 --> 05:29.020
go heavier today.

160
05:29.040 --> 05:29.480
Look.

161
05:29.580 --> 05:32.000
- All muscle, no strength to defend yourself! - Ow!

162
05:32.020 --> 05:33.140
Go heavier, got it?!

163
05:33.159 --> 05:34.460
I have muscles,

164
05:34.480 --> 05:35.970
but the thief had a knife!

165
05:36.100 --> 05:37.260
How's that my fault?

166
05:38.330 --> 05:40.510
He got robbed right outside our dorm.

167
05:41.280 --> 05:42.280
I don't care.

168
05:42.570 --> 05:44.200
The dorm has to take responsibility.

169
05:45.040 --> 05:47.030
So, are you gonna compensate my son or what?!

170
05:47.850 --> 05:48.920
If you're not gonna pay,

171
05:49.030 --> 05:50.730
then lower

172
05:50.750 --> 05:51.810
my rent.

173
05:52.070 --> 05:54.500
Whoa, Auntie Duang.

174
05:54.520 --> 05:57.190
I'm truly sorry. We really don't have enough security guards.

175
05:57.210 --> 05:59.620
We'll hire more security guards,

176
05:59.640 --> 06:02.820
but we'll have to raise the rent too, Auntie Duang.

177
06:05.750 --> 06:06.560
Hey,

178
06:06.580 --> 06:07.990
why would you do that?

179
06:08.010 --> 06:09.690
Keeping our dorm safe

180
06:09.710 --> 06:11.500
takes all of us working together.

181
06:11.520 --> 06:13.310
No need to hire more security guards. It's a waste!

182
06:15.510 --> 06:16.840
Oh, that's a relief.

183
06:16.860 --> 06:18.780
You're taking your brother to file a police report, right?

184
06:18.810 --> 06:20.550
Take him too, then.

185
06:20.900 --> 06:21.560
Mm.

186
06:21.990 --> 06:23.760
Lieutenant Dome is clocking out.

187
06:23.820 --> 06:25.110
Now it's time for...

188
06:25.130 --> 06:26.790
"Queen Dominiga" to entertain you!

189
06:27.990 --> 06:28.990
Are you ready?

190
06:29.010 --> 06:30.340
I'm so ready, Mama!

191
06:30.360 --> 06:31.530
Let's go, Daisy.

192
06:31.550 --> 06:32.300
Follow me!

193
06:32.490 --> 06:33.490
Hurry up.

194
06:33.510 --> 06:34.650
- Let's go. How fabulous. - Let's go.

195
06:34.670 --> 06:35.810
You're so annoying.

196
06:36.680 --> 06:38.670
So? What do you think?

197
06:38.690 --> 06:41.110
The kids in my dorm

198
06:41.310 --> 06:43.670
are fabulous, are they not?

199
06:45.890 --> 06:46.850
Whoa.

200
06:46.870 --> 06:48.320
That's so deep...deep...deep...

201
06:48.400 --> 06:49.480
Hello...lo...lo...

202
06:49.490 --> 06:50.650
Whoa, so deep.

203
06:50.909 --> 06:52.080
Hey, it's so deep.

204
06:52.100 --> 06:54.200
If you accidentally fall, no one would know.

205
06:54.370 --> 06:55.930
♫I-I-I-I'm not scared♫

206
06:55.950 --> 06:56.490
Hey!

207
06:56.510 --> 06:57.470
Hurry up.

208
06:57.480 --> 06:58.640
I'm hungry, and it's hot.

209
06:58.659 --> 06:59.990
♫Wait a minute, alright, alright?♫

210
07:00.010 --> 07:00.590
Hey!

211
07:00.610 --> 07:01.910
Just say it. No need to sing.

212
07:01.990 --> 07:03.050
♫I don't know how to say it♫

213
07:03.060 --> 07:04.090
- ♫How to say it♫ - But I know how to kick you.

214
07:06.570 --> 07:07.210
Dawin!

215
07:07.230 --> 07:08.740
Couldn't you catch me with your hands?!

216
07:08.760 --> 07:09.720
My hands?

217
07:09.740 --> 07:10.200
Look!

218
07:12.070 --> 07:13.150
Whoa, that's so red.

219
07:13.170 --> 07:14.900
You were cheering for a football team, huh?

220
07:14.920 --> 07:16.300
Are you cheering for the Red Devils or the Reds?

221
07:16.320 --> 07:17.530
The Red Brat!

222
07:17.930 --> 07:19.900
I told Daeng to fix my water heater yesterday.

223
07:20.010 --> 07:20.870
You call this fixed?

224
07:20.890 --> 07:22.350
Hot water came out of the sink

225
07:22.380 --> 07:23.340
and burned my hands like this!

226
07:23.490 --> 07:24.830
You told me to fix it,

227
07:24.850 --> 07:25.750
but you never said

228
07:25.770 --> 07:27.500
which hole the water should come out of.

229
07:27.650 --> 07:28.450
What? Hey...

230
07:28.470 --> 07:29.870
You did this on purpose.

231
07:30.190 --> 07:31.100
Now my hands are like this.

232
07:31.120 --> 07:32.300
How am I supposed to work?

233
07:32.409 --> 07:33.470
That's a good thing, isn't it?

234
07:34.070 --> 07:35.370
Now you won't be able to trick anyone else

235
07:35.390 --> 07:36.790
with your fortune-telling!

236
07:36.890 --> 07:37.690
Fine!

237
07:38.290 --> 07:39.860
Get ready to lose your job,

238
07:39.890 --> 07:40.990
unhandyman.

239
07:41.190 --> 07:42.130
Just wait until

240
07:42.150 --> 07:44.580
Danis hears about this. I wonder what she'll say.

241
07:46.730 --> 07:47.260
Mr. Dawin,

242
07:47.270 --> 07:48.190
please calm down!

243
07:48.210 --> 07:49.230
Mr. Dawin!

244
07:49.250 --> 07:50.400
Hurry up and apologize to him.

245
07:50.420 --> 07:51.060
What are you waiting for?!

246
07:51.080 --> 07:52.870
♫I'm still free, you know?♫

247
07:52.890 --> 07:53.950
Hey! Come here.

248
07:53.960 --> 07:54.760
Go apologize to him!

249
08:09.620 --> 08:10.900
Whoa!

250
08:10.920 --> 08:12.000
Fabulous, Mama!

251
08:12.230 --> 08:14.020
Come help me first. My back hurts.

252
08:14.040 --> 08:15.610
Don't just sit there saying "fabulous." Come on.

253
08:15.640 --> 08:16.350
Okay, sit down first.

254
08:16.360 --> 08:17.590
Ow, ow, ow, my back...

255
08:17.600 --> 08:18.670
- Thank you, dear. - Are you alright?

256
08:18.740 --> 08:19.420
Dobby,

257
08:19.440 --> 08:20.340
you're here anyway.

258
08:20.360 --> 08:21.990
Ask them

259
08:22.010 --> 08:23.340
if they know Gaysorn.

260
08:25.390 --> 08:26.480
Um... Dome?

261
08:27.130 --> 08:29.730
Call me "Queen Dominiga."

262
08:30.930 --> 08:32.980
- Queen Dominiga... - That's right.

263
08:33.000 --> 08:33.860
- Yes. - Fabulous.

264
08:33.880 --> 08:34.669
I want to know

265
08:34.690 --> 08:36.390
if you have a relative named Gaysorn.

266
08:36.409 --> 08:38.190
My grandpa is looking for his friend.

267
08:38.409 --> 08:39.760
A relative named Gaysorn...

268
08:39.990 --> 08:41.159
I don't have a relative with that name.

269
08:41.260 --> 08:42.510
But if it's a friend, I do have one.

270
08:44.090 --> 08:44.920
Look, there!

271
08:45.310 --> 08:46.950
"Queen Tiger Pollen."

272
08:47.280 --> 08:47.790
See?

273
08:47.810 --> 08:50.150
It means "Gaysorn (pollen) of a tiger lily."

274
08:52.430 --> 08:53.430
Does this work for you?

275
08:54.670 --> 08:56.120
You saw my show earlier, didn't you?

276
08:56.140 --> 08:57.140
You're so cool.

277
08:57.160 --> 08:58.270
If I can do that

278
08:58.300 --> 08:59.490
on my audition day,

279
08:59.680 --> 09:00.640
I'll definitely get the role.

280
09:00.760 --> 09:01.700
Alright, stand up.

281
09:01.720 --> 09:02.720
- Stand up, dear. - Stand up.

282
09:02.750 --> 09:03.630
Stand... You, too.

283
09:03.660 --> 09:05.020
- Oh, I have to stand, too? - Stand up.

284
09:05.100 --> 09:06.160
Point your toe.

285
09:06.180 --> 09:07.220
Both of you.

286
09:07.250 --> 09:08.250
Look up.

287
09:08.270 --> 09:09.720
Keep it up, look straight.

288
09:09.740 --> 09:11.090
Very nice, dear.

289
09:11.150 --> 09:11.880
Picture yourself as...

290
09:11.910 --> 09:13.130
a diva.

291
09:14.350 --> 09:15.510
How about this?

292
09:15.690 --> 09:16.800
You mamas can practice

293
09:16.820 --> 09:18.110
while I'll excuse myself.

294
09:18.130 --> 09:19.340
- Hey, wait! - Hey, wait, wait, wait.

295
09:19.360 --> 09:20.460
You have to be here with me.

296
09:20.750 --> 09:22.150
That way, I'll know...

297
09:22.160 --> 09:23.510
if I'm fully immersed in my role as Daisy.

298
09:23.520 --> 09:26.100
You're splendid in this role, Daisy!

299
09:26.120 --> 09:27.390
I haven't even started yet.

300
09:28.470 --> 09:30.870
- Dome! - Oh, no...

301
09:31.770 --> 09:33.450
The outfit you asked me to fix is ready.

302
09:33.470 --> 09:34.300
Ooh, here it is!

303
09:34.330 --> 09:36.200
And this is the food you ordered from my mom.

304
09:36.210 --> 09:37.990
- Oh, I was just getting hungry... - Oh, wow!

305
09:38.670 --> 09:39.560
You have an audience now.

306
09:39.660 --> 09:40.850
These two

307
09:40.870 --> 09:42.330
will stay to help you,

308
09:42.430 --> 09:44.580
while I have a matter to tend to.

309
09:44.600 --> 09:47.120
Ms. Danis has some paperwork for me to sign.

310
09:47.130 --> 09:48.340
Oh, I have a lot to do.

311
09:48.360 --> 09:49.480
So I'll have to...

312
09:50.270 --> 09:51.280
take my leave.

313
09:51.630 --> 09:52.360
Take care of Dax for me.

314
09:52.490 --> 09:53.110
What?

315
09:53.350 --> 09:53.990
Bye-bye.

316
09:54.010 --> 09:55.130
Oh, please...

317
09:55.140 --> 09:55.980
Leave him.

318
09:56.050 --> 09:57.780
You still have time, so come help me with my student.

319
09:57.810 --> 09:59.090
- Here. Come. - Come here, quick.

320
09:59.110 --> 09:59.960
Come here.

321
10:00.010 --> 10:01.260
Come, come, come.

322
10:01.280 --> 10:01.900
Come here.

323
10:01.920 --> 10:02.860
Don't just stand there.

324
10:02.880 --> 10:03.720
- Come. - Walk!

325
10:03.740 --> 10:04.460
I can't with you, handsome.

326
10:04.490 --> 10:05.700
Why? Are your muscles too heavy?

327
10:05.880 --> 10:06.880
Okay,

328
10:07.010 --> 10:07.770
time for a vocal warm-up.

329
10:07.780 --> 10:09.470
Let's start by saying...

330
10:09.490 --> 10:12.500
♫Wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa♫

331
10:14.030 --> 10:14.870
Daisy, go.

332
10:14.890 --> 10:18.080
- ♫Wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa♫ - ♫Wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa♫

333
10:18.100 --> 10:19.590
You two, don't just stand there.

334
10:19.610 --> 10:21.040
All together now.

335
10:21.060 --> 10:24.660
- ♫Wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa♫ - ♫Wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa, wa♫

336
10:24.680 --> 10:25.980
Good!

337
10:26.330 --> 10:27.430
One more time!

338
10:27.680 --> 10:28.680
Sign here.

339
10:28.690 --> 10:30.230
That's all, Mr. Drip.

340
10:31.800 --> 10:32.700
Here you go.

341
10:32.720 --> 10:34.390
Thank you so much, Mr. Drip.

342
10:34.690 --> 10:36.470
I officially welcome you

343
10:36.500 --> 10:39.630
to 'the D Dorm.'

344
10:39.650 --> 10:41.150
Thank you for helping me.

345
10:41.170 --> 10:43.950
I'll pay for your meal, then.

346
10:44.590 --> 10:47.150
You're welcome. Don't mind if I do, then.

347
10:48.180 --> 10:49.340
Auntie Duang!

348
10:49.360 --> 10:50.120
Yes?

349
10:50.140 --> 10:51.070
Check, please?

350
10:51.990 --> 10:53.160
One hundred and twenty baht.

351
10:53.510 --> 10:54.510
Cool!

352
10:55.710 --> 10:57.500
Are you dressing up as a milestone?

353
10:58.390 --> 10:59.350
Whoa, that mouth...

354
10:59.950 --> 11:01.860
Asking me to burn your room down, huh?

355
11:02.470 --> 11:03.470
Burn his room down?

356
11:03.720 --> 11:05.950
If you do that, the fire's gonna reach your room.

357
11:05.970 --> 11:07.900
Because your rooms are right next to each other.

358
11:08.110 --> 11:08.980
Hey!

359
11:09.050 --> 11:10.430
Our stores are close,

360
11:10.590 --> 11:11.660
and now we live next to each other?!

361
11:11.730 --> 11:12.280
Hey,

362
11:12.560 --> 11:14.230
when are you gonna stop pestering me, hm?

363
11:17.380 --> 11:18.150
One hundred and twenty baht.

364
11:18.170 --> 11:18.810
Yes, Auntie.

365
11:21.170 --> 11:22.260
Danis!

366
11:22.400 --> 11:24.070
You'll have to find a new handyman for this dorm.

367
11:24.520 --> 11:25.110
Why?

368
11:25.130 --> 11:26.980
Handyman Daeng purposely pranked me

369
11:27.000 --> 11:28.860
by hooking up hot water to my sink.

370
11:28.880 --> 11:30.310
See how it burned my hands?!

371
11:30.880 --> 11:31.730
Whoa...

372
11:32.200 --> 11:33.170
Ms. Danis,

373
11:34.630 --> 11:35.830
if you're gonna kick someone out,

374
11:35.880 --> 11:37.570
kick this scammer tenant out!

375
11:38.140 --> 11:40.470
Letting him scam people with fortune-telling like this

376
11:40.490 --> 11:41.550
is giving the dorm a bad name!

377
11:41.570 --> 11:42.360
Oh!

378
11:42.390 --> 11:43.550
You're the scammer!

379
11:43.570 --> 11:45.090
You burned me with hot water,

380
11:45.110 --> 11:46.430
clearly trying to kill me!

381
11:47.300 --> 11:48.550
Ugh! Enough with the two of you.

382
11:48.560 --> 11:49.350
You're fighting again.

383
11:49.710 --> 11:50.740
When? Tell me when?!

384
11:50.760 --> 11:52.200
When will you stop fighting?!

385
11:52.210 --> 11:53.210
What a headache!

386
11:53.240 --> 11:57.270
♫There has to be a day, some day♫

387
11:57.410 --> 11:59.670
♫Two days, three days♫

388
11:59.760 --> 12:01.690
♫Four days, five days♫

389
12:01.810 --> 12:04.270
♫Six days, seven days♫

390
12:04.290 --> 12:05.700
Greetings to my fans.

391
12:05.780 --> 12:07.270
- This way! - This way!

392
12:07.640 --> 12:09.200
There's a reason I'm singing.

393
12:09.520 --> 12:11.630
I was trying to cheer you up, Ms. Danis.

394
12:11.810 --> 12:12.290
Oh?

395
12:12.400 --> 12:13.470
You're tired, aren't you?

396
12:13.490 --> 12:14.240
Yes.

397
12:14.260 --> 12:15.200
I'm tired as well!

398
12:15.220 --> 12:16.310
Just by walking outside,

399
12:16.320 --> 12:17.040
I can hear people singing...

400
12:17.070 --> 12:18.090
♫Thrust a little, black vest♫

401
12:18.100 --> 12:19.160
♫Thrust, thrust, black vest♫

402
12:19.480 --> 12:21.560
I was thrusting nonstop, so I'm tired.

403
12:21.780 --> 12:23.450
And now I have to see the two of them fighting.

404
12:23.470 --> 12:24.390
Today is the day

405
12:24.700 --> 12:26.190
I put an end to this.

406
12:26.600 --> 12:27.480
Daeng,

407
12:28.970 --> 12:30.440
will you stop picking fights with Mr. Dawin?

408
12:30.580 --> 12:31.290
Never!

409
12:32.800 --> 12:33.640
Mr. Dawin,

410
12:33.750 --> 12:35.310
will you stop fighting with my brother?

411
12:35.500 --> 12:36.370
I'll stop

412
12:36.380 --> 12:38.030
when your brother stops.

413
12:40.000 --> 12:41.380
We're in the same dorm.

414
12:41.390 --> 12:42.400
Why don't we love each other?

415
12:42.420 --> 12:43.850
I don't love you.

416
12:45.550 --> 12:47.910
I'll ask you two one last time.

417
12:48.720 --> 12:50.560
Will you change your mind?!

418
12:50.580 --> 12:51.660
- No! - No!

419
12:54.230 --> 12:55.980
Then it can't be helped.

420
13:00.830 --> 13:01.720
What is this?!

421
13:01.750 --> 13:02.570
- Ow! - Ow!

422
13:02.590 --> 13:03.900
- Let go! - Ow!

423
13:03.930 --> 13:04.780
Stop. Stop right there.

424
13:05.050 --> 13:05.620
Guard Dum!

425
13:05.640 --> 13:07.290
I can report you to the police

426
13:07.310 --> 13:08.680
for unlawful confinement!

427
13:08.700 --> 13:09.460
How will you do that

428
13:09.470 --> 13:11.140
when your phone is right here?

429
13:12.450 --> 13:13.870
The police station is ten kilometers from here.

430
13:13.890 --> 13:14.730
Feel free to shout

431
13:14.740 --> 13:15.610
if you want a sore throat.

432
13:16.080 --> 13:17.740
How about this? If you want me to let you go,

433
13:17.760 --> 13:18.960
both of you will have to promise me

434
13:18.980 --> 13:20.430
that you'll stop fighting.

435
13:20.480 --> 13:21.190
- Never! - Never!

436
13:21.830 --> 13:23.200
Good! Stay there, then.

437
13:23.220 --> 13:25.530
It's like I have two poodles welcoming my customers.

438
13:27.640 --> 13:29.410
I tease you because I love you.

439
13:29.630 --> 13:30.410
Whoa...

440
13:30.420 --> 13:32.310
You shouldn't stand too close, then.

441
13:32.710 --> 13:34.740
Or the poodles will pee on the milestone.

442
13:34.770 --> 13:35.840
I tease you because I love you.

443
13:35.850 --> 13:37.380
Oh...I got a taste of my own medicine.

444
13:38.070 --> 13:39.350
I'll have to ask you

445
13:39.370 --> 13:40.580
to keep an eye on those two.

446
13:40.590 --> 13:41.800
- Yes. - If they're still fighting,

447
13:41.830 --> 13:43.260
just keep interpreting them.

448
13:43.950 --> 13:44.840
Interpret what?

449
13:44.860 --> 13:45.470
"Intertwined."

450
13:45.490 --> 13:46.960
Aha...

451
13:46.980 --> 13:48.200
I should get back to work now.

452
13:48.220 --> 13:49.770
- Yes. - Don't miss me too much.

453
13:50.480 --> 13:51.550
- Yes. - Ugh!

454
13:52.340 --> 13:53.340
Dum!

455
13:53.360 --> 13:54.990
- What, Daeng? - I'm your big brother!

456
13:55.800 --> 13:57.110
- Let me go! - Danis!

457
13:57.140 --> 13:58.200
Ms. Danis!

458
13:58.220 --> 13:59.520
If someone has a problem

459
13:59.530 --> 14:00.830
or something breaks,

460
14:00.840 --> 14:01.850
who's gonna fix it?

461
14:02.460 --> 14:04.250
Anyone but you, unhandyman!

462
14:04.270 --> 14:04.640
Oh...

463
14:04.660 --> 14:06.030
It's you, con artist!

464
14:06.040 --> 14:06.660
It's you!

465
14:06.670 --> 14:07.790
- Take this! - Don't touch me!

466
14:07.820 --> 14:09.410
- Ugh! - Oh...

467
14:09.520 --> 14:10.830
You won't be released tomorrow at this rate!

468
14:11.790 --> 14:12.620
You!

469
14:12.640 --> 14:14.430
- You were just making things up - It's you!

470
14:14.440 --> 14:15.550
when you read the cards for Mr. Aoftion!

471
14:15.570 --> 14:17.040
Oh, you're gorgeous, dear.

472
14:17.060 --> 14:18.560
- Oh, I'm excited. - So cute.

473
14:18.580 --> 14:20.240
You're stunning!

474
14:21.190 --> 14:22.430
Look in the mirror.

475
14:22.790 --> 14:23.940
- Look at yourself. - Oh!

476
14:23.960 --> 14:25.800
- So? Do you like it? - It's so pretty.

477
14:28.110 --> 14:30.240
Daisy, let me tell you something.

478
14:30.380 --> 14:31.660
Wearing makeup

479
14:31.690 --> 14:33.600
is like burying your old identity

480
14:33.620 --> 14:36.490
and rebuilding your ideal identity in its place.

481
14:36.580 --> 14:37.250
Do you understand?

482
14:37.270 --> 14:38.110
Yes.

483
14:38.230 --> 14:40.590
With those huge lashes, what are you planning to dress as?

484
14:40.610 --> 14:41.500
A Venus flytrap?

485
14:41.710 --> 14:42.300
- Oh. - Hey.

486
14:42.320 --> 14:43.650
- I'll slap that mouth of yours. - How dare you.

487
14:43.670 --> 14:44.940
- Hey! - That hurts!

488
14:44.990 --> 14:47.910
That's the style of drag makeup.

489
14:48.750 --> 14:51.270
Stop eating clean and try to eat more food for your brain, Dollar.

490
14:51.290 --> 14:51.930
Oh, how dare you!

491
14:51.950 --> 14:54.630
- That's right. Get omega three, six, nine, eleven - Hey...

492
14:54.650 --> 14:56.080
- Yes. - to make you smarter.

493
14:57.030 --> 14:58.120
But if they're that huge,

494
14:58.210 --> 14:59.100
will you be able to see?

495
14:59.750 --> 15:00.910
If you're that curious,

496
15:00.930 --> 15:01.980
why don't you give it a try?

497
15:02.990 --> 15:05.140
Be a model for my student, why don't you?

498
15:05.160 --> 15:06.000
Dolly, go.

499
15:06.020 --> 15:06.620
Hey.

500
15:06.640 --> 15:07.800
No need to argue.

501
15:07.820 --> 15:08.710
You, come here.

502
15:09.320 --> 15:10.350
Or next time,

503
15:10.370 --> 15:12.390
I won't exchange my shifts with you.

504
15:12.870 --> 15:13.830
Fine.

505
15:13.850 --> 15:15.310
- Go on. - Come here.

506
15:15.330 --> 15:16.170
- Hey, dear. - Yes?

507
15:16.190 --> 15:17.060
You'll get to see

508
15:17.080 --> 15:18.940
what real drag is like.

509
15:19.890 --> 15:21.870
You can't put on the lashes

510
15:21.890 --> 15:23.300
carelessly, alright?

511
15:23.320 --> 15:25.420
You have to make it captivating.

512
15:25.450 --> 15:25.880
Of course.

513
15:25.900 --> 15:26.900
- Understood? - Yes.

514
15:30.800 --> 15:33.710
Did you understand everything I taught you?

515
15:33.730 --> 15:34.560
I got it.

516
15:34.580 --> 15:35.620
Good job.

517
15:35.640 --> 15:36.910
Then I'll excuse myself for a bit.

518
15:36.930 --> 15:38.420
- Okay. - Good.

519
15:39.840 --> 15:40.350
Come here.

520
15:40.690 --> 15:41.630
Excuse me.

521
15:42.280 --> 15:43.600
- Come right here. - Is this a good idea?

522
15:43.620 --> 15:44.550
- Come here - Is this a good idea?

523
15:44.570 --> 15:45.850
- Sit, sit, sit. - Um, I've never...

524
15:45.870 --> 15:47.410
Sit down. Give it a try.

525
15:47.890 --> 15:48.890
Let me see.

526
15:53.110 --> 15:54.110
All done.

527
15:54.350 --> 15:55.880
Look how beautiful they are.

528
15:55.980 --> 15:57.960
- Oh, wow. - It suits you very well.

529
15:58.300 --> 15:59.930
But why do my eyes...

530
16:00.210 --> 16:02.190
feel irritated?

531
16:03.070 --> 16:04.380
Why is that?

532
16:04.880 --> 16:07.420
When I did it, it felt cool, like normal.

533
16:07.440 --> 16:08.700
Ow...

534
16:09.030 --> 16:09.820
- Wait... - Let me see.

535
16:09.840 --> 16:11.120
- Let me take a look at the glue - Here.

536
16:13.120 --> 16:15.140
Wait, this isn't eyelash glue!

537
16:15.170 --> 16:15.920
- Huh? - Huh?

538
16:15.940 --> 16:17.030
Oh, gosh!

539
16:17.050 --> 16:18.880
- Take it off, quick! - Oh, no!

540
16:19.210 --> 16:20.640
- Slowly, slowly. - Pull it gently.

541
16:25.350 --> 16:26.310
Where's Dome?

542
16:29.210 --> 16:32.190
[Din, occupation: police officer (Dome's older brother)] อาชีพ

543
16:32.590 --> 16:33.500
Din...

544
16:33.520 --> 16:34.320
How did you get here?

545
16:34.340 --> 16:35.870
Why did you quit being a cop?

546
16:35.890 --> 16:37.310
Well, I didn't want to be a cop,

547
16:37.340 --> 16:39.260
but I want to be a drag queen.

548
16:49.300 --> 16:50.230
Oh, wow.

549
16:50.250 --> 16:50.950
Hey, Grandpa.

550
16:50.970 --> 16:52.960
Seriously, if I burn these, will you receive them?

551
16:52.980 --> 16:53.940
Probably.

552
16:54.340 --> 16:55.070
Want a pair of glasses?

553
16:55.950 --> 16:56.360
Here.

554
16:59.290 --> 17:00.830
It didn't work, Grandpa.

555
17:00.850 --> 17:03.080
Put in more effort!

556
17:03.100 --> 17:04.960
You cannot do it half-heartedly.

557
17:05.030 --> 17:07.950
Focus on sending it to me.

558
17:08.109 --> 17:08.960
It is that simple.

559
17:08.980 --> 17:10.740
But I do not want those things anymore.

560
17:10.760 --> 17:12.829
I just want the mobile phone.

561
17:12.859 --> 17:14.109
- The phone? - Yeah.

562
17:14.130 --> 17:14.730
What for?

563
17:14.750 --> 17:16.550
Maybe I will use it to watch vertical dramas!

564
17:16.569 --> 17:17.630
Oh, sarcastic, huh?

565
17:17.650 --> 17:20.599
I just want to call my friends who passed.

566
17:20.619 --> 17:22.660
I am tired of talking to you all the time.

567
17:22.680 --> 17:23.920
Oh, wow. Okay.

568
17:23.940 --> 17:25.810
I'm tired of that, too. Alright.

569
17:25.940 --> 17:26.980
I'll send it to you.

570
17:27.290 --> 17:29.040
Buddham aranam dhammam nasangham talanam.

571
17:30.420 --> 17:31.210
Huh?

572
17:31.230 --> 17:32.320
Throwit when yu ar done.

573
17:32.350 --> 17:33.240
Huh? There's a chant, too?

574
17:33.260 --> 17:34.640
Throw it when you are done!

575
17:36.580 --> 17:37.500
- Wait, what?! - Whoa!

576
17:40.160 --> 17:41.500
Don't you think the outfits look similar?

577
17:41.520 --> 17:42.080
Yeah...

578
17:42.310 --> 17:43.310
- Whoa! - Whoa!

579
17:43.330 --> 17:44.470
Hey, what's going on?!

580
17:45.490 --> 17:46.650
- Oh. Whoa. - Oh.

581
17:47.430 --> 17:48.060
Hey.

582
17:49.220 --> 17:50.000
- Dax. - Ow.

583
17:50.020 --> 17:51.070
What happened, Dax?

584
17:51.090 --> 17:52.360
Well,

585
17:52.380 --> 17:54.220
- Mama Moniga - Is it dirty?

586
17:54.240 --> 17:56.390
wants to quit being a cop and be a drag queen instead.

587
17:56.410 --> 17:57.830
But their brother wouldn't have it,

588
17:57.930 --> 17:59.140
so he came to their room.

589
17:59.160 --> 18:00.480
Yelling and making a huge fuss.

590
18:00.500 --> 18:01.270
He nearly brought the room down!

591
18:01.290 --> 18:02.650
You were a cop.

592
18:02.670 --> 18:04.550
Why did you quit, Dome?

593
18:04.620 --> 18:05.700
- Look at these outfits. - Don't pick them up.

594
18:08.260 --> 18:10.280
I won't let you do this kind of nonsense again.

595
18:10.300 --> 18:11.550
Nonsense?

596
18:11.770 --> 18:13.210
This is the job I love, Din!

597
18:13.420 --> 18:14.860
And does the job you love

598
18:14.880 --> 18:15.920
pay the bills?

599
18:16.600 --> 18:17.830
You'll end up depending on me

600
18:17.850 --> 18:19.020
or our parents!

601
18:19.310 --> 18:20.310
Hey...

602
18:21.450 --> 18:23.030
Calm down, Din.

603
18:23.050 --> 18:24.240
This is the path

604
18:24.260 --> 18:25.580
Dome chose.

605
18:25.600 --> 18:26.410
Stop talking!

606
18:27.070 --> 18:28.000
You, too.

607
18:28.020 --> 18:29.040
Who picked those lashes for you?

608
18:31.150 --> 18:32.480
Seeing them really pisses me off.

609
18:33.640 --> 18:34.580
Picture this:

610
18:34.870 --> 18:36.640
if your brother quit being a cop

611
18:36.800 --> 18:38.240
to do something like this,

612
18:38.270 --> 18:39.780
would you be okay with that, Dolly?

613
18:44.080 --> 18:45.150
I'd love that.

614
18:45.690 --> 18:47.430
Dollar will get to be pretty.

615
18:47.450 --> 18:48.500
Dolly!

616
18:48.680 --> 18:49.660
You stop talking.

617
18:49.680 --> 18:50.350
Stop right there.

618
18:50.520 --> 18:51.800
But to be honest,

619
18:51.930 --> 18:53.560
drag queen performers

620
18:53.580 --> 18:54.970
make a lot of money.

621
18:54.990 --> 18:56.430
Especially the top performers,

622
18:56.460 --> 18:58.180
who get paid around a hundred thousand a month.

623
18:59.890 --> 19:01.890
Do you think becoming a top performer

624
19:01.910 --> 19:02.910
is easy?

625
19:04.330 --> 19:06.580
Not everyone who does this will end up successful!

626
19:06.610 --> 19:08.750
I know it's not easy,

627
19:09.830 --> 19:12.550
but can't I choose to live my life the way I want?

628
19:13.690 --> 19:14.790
This is your life,

629
19:14.810 --> 19:15.890
not a pair of sandals.

630
19:15.910 --> 19:17.690
You cannot just keep changing things.

631
19:17.710 --> 19:20.190
Making the wrong choice will ruin your life!

632
19:21.800 --> 19:22.800
Dome,

633
19:23.620 --> 19:25.110
you have a bright future.

634
19:26.750 --> 19:28.720
So why are you risking your future...

635
19:28.740 --> 19:30.010
with something like this?

636
19:33.530 --> 19:35.000
At least I'm happy.

637
19:36.190 --> 19:37.480
You're my brother.

638
19:38.200 --> 19:39.890
Shouldn't you be happy

639
19:40.590 --> 19:41.750
when I'm happy?

640
19:47.000 --> 19:48.510
This is the last time I'm gonna say this.

641
19:50.200 --> 19:51.680
If you're still going to quit,

642
19:53.000 --> 19:53.990
then don't call me your brother anymore.

643
19:57.100 --> 19:58.100
Din.

644
20:00.810 --> 20:01.710
Dome...

645
20:02.400 --> 20:03.480
Fine.

646
20:04.010 --> 20:05.080
Hey, Dome.

647
20:05.100 --> 20:05.780
Dome...

648
20:08.600 --> 20:09.480
Dome!

649
20:09.690 --> 20:11.090
- Dome, wait! - Dome!

650
20:15.250 --> 20:16.380
Whoa,

651
20:16.410 --> 20:18.490
do they really have to cut ties over this?

652
20:18.510 --> 20:19.200
Yeah...

653
20:19.220 --> 20:20.020
if I were him,

654
20:20.050 --> 20:23.090
I would not just cut ties with them, I am telling you.

655
20:23.110 --> 20:24.750
I will wait for them to get what they deserve!

656
20:24.780 --> 20:26.860
We are older and wiser.

657
20:26.880 --> 20:28.750
You should listen to what we say!

658
20:29.250 --> 20:30.710
- Get what they deserve? - Mm.

659
20:31.000 --> 20:32.550
Like what you did to Mom?

660
20:35.670 --> 20:36.380
Dobby...

661
20:36.400 --> 20:37.510
Who were you talking to?

662
20:37.830 --> 20:38.830
Your grandpa?

663
20:38.890 --> 20:40.430
It is not the same.

664
20:40.590 --> 20:42.090
Those brothers are fighting,

665
20:42.120 --> 20:43.290
and so are grandpa and grandson.

666
20:43.310 --> 20:44.450
Daisy has a headache!

667
20:44.470 --> 20:45.720
Daisy can't take it anymore!

668
20:47.130 --> 20:47.890
Here.

669
20:48.470 --> 20:49.470
What?!

670
20:49.490 --> 20:51.180
I ordered pad kra pao, Auntie.

671
20:51.600 --> 20:52.560
Why did you give me khanom jeen?

672
20:52.580 --> 20:55.150
Hey, you're just a prisoner. What right do you have to choose?

673
20:55.170 --> 20:57.890
I told her to make khanom jeen for you.

674
20:57.910 --> 20:58.910
Here.

675
20:59.490 --> 21:00.860
Your spoon.

676
21:00.880 --> 21:01.760
Your fork.

677
21:01.780 --> 21:03.100
If you don't want to starve,

678
21:03.130 --> 21:05.700
take turns feeding each other, alright?

679
21:06.380 --> 21:07.280
Come on!

680
21:07.300 --> 21:08.230
Ms. Danis,

681
21:08.250 --> 21:10.230
I'm forced to stay handcuffed to him,

682
21:10.250 --> 21:12.490
and now you're forcing me to feed him, too?

683
21:12.510 --> 21:13.270
Yes.

684
21:14.310 --> 21:16.190
Just treat each other better.

685
21:16.210 --> 21:17.970
- Mm. - And stop fighting already.

686
21:17.990 --> 21:18.990
Never!

687
21:19.750 --> 21:20.750
I can take care of myself.

688
21:21.300 --> 21:22.470
I don't need his help!

689
21:32.600 --> 21:34.730
That's what you get for relying only on luck!

690
21:34.750 --> 21:36.230
Not your brain.

691
21:36.310 --> 21:37.990
You have to use a fork!

692
21:41.750 --> 21:42.320
Look.

693
21:44.940 --> 21:45.710
Dream on!

694
21:49.350 --> 21:50.000
There!

695
21:50.950 --> 21:52.460
Mr. Big Brain,

696
21:52.480 --> 21:54.860
how are you gonna use your fork now?

697
21:56.090 --> 21:56.730
What are you looking at?

698
21:57.100 --> 21:58.600
Want me to feed you? Hm?

699
22:01.370 --> 22:03.210
- Seriously, - Hey!

700
22:03.230 --> 22:04.520
- when are these two - I didn't get to eat...

701
22:04.540 --> 22:06.350
- so you don't get to either! - gonna stop fighting?

702
22:06.370 --> 22:07.150
Auntie,

703
22:07.170 --> 22:08.990
it won't be long until they drop the tough act.

704
22:09.010 --> 22:11.190
They'll give up soon enough.

705
22:11.700 --> 22:14.290
But they're being silly and now fighting with utensils.

706
22:14.490 --> 22:15.490
That's true, Auntie.

707
22:16.190 --> 22:17.470
Did they watch too many movies?

708
22:17.490 --> 22:19.090
Ugh...

709
22:21.810 --> 22:22.770
Stop.

710
22:23.830 --> 22:26.520
[The D Dorm]

711
22:29.710 --> 22:30.650
Oh, wow!

712
22:31.290 --> 22:32.180
So refreshing!

713
22:32.890 --> 22:34.860
Very refreshing.

714
22:35.290 --> 22:36.150
Oh?

715
22:36.170 --> 22:36.980
What are you looking at?

716
22:37.010 --> 22:38.180
Are you thirsty?

717
22:38.600 --> 22:39.550
I'm not giving you this.

718
22:40.090 --> 22:40.910
Hey...

719
22:41.280 --> 22:42.110
Ms. Danis,

720
22:42.750 --> 22:43.750
look at my lips.

721
22:43.770 --> 22:45.390
They're so dry.

722
22:45.540 --> 22:46.600
I'll have to say...

723
22:47.150 --> 22:49.470
♫Water, I need...♫

724
22:49.490 --> 22:50.360
Ugh!

725
22:50.980 --> 22:51.680
Why are you singing?

726
22:51.830 --> 22:53.230
The more you talk, the more thirsty you'll get.

727
22:53.610 --> 22:54.510
Danis,

728
22:54.620 --> 22:56.490
starving us is a bit cruel, don't you think?

729
22:56.520 --> 22:57.980
When will you let us go?

730
22:58.300 --> 22:59.000
Oh!

731
22:59.430 --> 23:00.430
Then make up already.

732
23:00.590 --> 23:01.150
- Never! - Never!

733
23:01.190 --> 23:01.890
Hey...

734
23:02.190 --> 23:03.370
Keep on starving, then.

735
23:04.350 --> 23:05.720
Danis, that's too cruel.

736
23:05.800 --> 23:07.150
Don't worry, boys.

737
23:07.170 --> 23:08.590
I'm not going to torture you.

738
23:08.610 --> 23:10.850
I bought you an ice cold coffee.

739
23:10.870 --> 23:12.000
Thank you, Auntie.

740
23:15.070 --> 23:15.710
Here.

741
23:17.080 --> 23:18.510
Why are the glasses empty?

742
23:18.530 --> 23:19.830
Where is the coffee?

743
23:19.970 --> 23:21.160
Here it is.

744
23:21.180 --> 23:23.200
Your coffee.

745
23:23.600 --> 23:24.690
Here.

746
23:26.870 --> 23:27.870
Whoa...

747
23:28.120 --> 23:29.520
You tied it like those food in plastic bags.

748
23:29.680 --> 23:31.470
How am I supposed to untie this?

749
23:31.620 --> 23:32.630
Help each other out, then.

750
23:33.120 --> 23:34.960
Lend each other a hand.

751
23:34.980 --> 23:36.270
The coffee you drink

752
23:36.290 --> 23:38.290
after facing obstacles and adversities

753
23:38.310 --> 23:41.040
will taste much sweeter, aromatic, and delicious.

754
23:41.730 --> 23:42.510
Hey, give me that!

755
23:43.080 --> 23:44.290
No need to untie it.

756
23:44.310 --> 23:45.250
I'll bite the bottom and drink!

757
23:46.770 --> 23:47.420
Give me that!

758
23:51.290 --> 23:53.240
Things don't seem to go as planned, Ms. Danis.

759
23:55.810 --> 23:56.810
I think...

760
23:57.010 --> 23:58.300
Should we leave them?

761
23:58.320 --> 24:00.910
From the looks of it, they won't make up with each other.

762
24:00.930 --> 24:02.040
No, Auntie.

763
24:02.060 --> 24:03.720
We've come this far.

764
24:03.740 --> 24:04.840
We'll have to see it to the end.

765
24:05.390 --> 24:06.980
After drinking that much,

766
24:07.000 --> 24:08.390
they'll have to pee.

767
24:08.410 --> 24:10.020
And if they still won't make up,

768
24:10.040 --> 24:11.490
we'll let them pee themselves.

769
24:11.500 --> 24:12.310
Hm?

770
24:12.330 --> 24:13.590
They can't do that. This is my restaurant.

771
24:13.610 --> 24:14.910
Well, it isn't my office.

772
24:14.920 --> 24:16.300
But won't it stink up my restaurant?

773
24:16.320 --> 24:17.860
It won't smell in my office.

774
24:17.880 --> 24:19.060
We can't hear you at all.

775
24:19.680 --> 24:20.210
Oh, oops.

776
24:20.220 --> 24:21.010
Oh...

777
24:25.520 --> 24:27.600
Dobby,

778
24:27.630 --> 24:31.780
why do you need to get into their business?

779
24:31.800 --> 24:33.470
I do not understand.

780
24:33.490 --> 24:36.580
Just let Dome feel guilty

781
24:36.600 --> 24:38.680
for not listening to his brother.

782
24:38.700 --> 24:39.820
Wait, Grandpa.

783
24:39.840 --> 24:40.870
Dome didn't do anything wrong.

784
24:41.100 --> 24:41.990
It's his life.

785
24:42.010 --> 24:43.610
He gets to choose how to live it.

786
24:43.630 --> 24:46.210
Being an older brother doesn't mean you can control his life.

787
24:46.230 --> 24:47.420
Nonsense!

788
24:48.090 --> 24:49.770
This is not "control."

789
24:49.790 --> 24:51.310
He just "means well."

790
24:53.520 --> 24:54.710
Who turned off the lights?!

791
24:54.730 --> 24:55.840
Who turned off the lights?!

792
24:56.400 --> 24:57.210
What...?

793
24:57.230 --> 24:57.870
Oh...

794
24:57.900 --> 25:00.490
Is this the pair of glasses you burned for me?

795
25:00.510 --> 25:01.830
Don't try to change the topic.

796
25:01.840 --> 25:04.280
Was pushing my parents out of your house

797
25:04.440 --> 25:05.880
your way of showing that you meant well?

798
25:05.900 --> 25:06.800
Yes!

799
25:07.130 --> 25:08.830
Your mom is stubborn!

800
25:08.850 --> 25:10.680
And look at her life now.

801
25:10.700 --> 25:12.150
She is drowning in debts!

802
25:12.170 --> 25:13.960
Owning a lousy restaurant.

803
25:13.980 --> 25:16.220
If she would just listen to me...

804
25:16.550 --> 25:18.600
she wouldn't end up pregnant by your dad!

805
25:20.330 --> 25:22.640
If she married the man I found for her,

806
25:22.660 --> 25:24.450
she would have prospered by now!

807
25:26.490 --> 25:27.690
Grandpa, when you say that,

808
25:28.910 --> 25:31.210
does it mean that I was born

809
25:32.030 --> 25:33.880
to hold Mom back from her fortune?

810
25:38.580 --> 25:40.490
Dobby, Dobby...

811
25:40.780 --> 25:42.300
Hey, I...

812
25:42.320 --> 25:43.530
I did not mean it like that.

813
25:43.540 --> 25:44.660
Calm down.

814
25:44.670 --> 25:45.350
What does it mean, then?

815
25:45.360 --> 25:45.980
Oh, f*ck!

816
25:45.990 --> 25:47.060
Did you insult me?!

817
25:49.470 --> 25:50.490
I'm not insulting you.

818
25:50.510 --> 25:51.270
I'm insulting your outfit.

819
25:54.240 --> 25:55.550
How the hell did it get here?

820
25:56.480 --> 25:57.400
- Whoa! - Whoa!

821
25:59.190 --> 26:00.630
Hey, Dobby!

822
26:00.730 --> 26:01.630
You...

823
26:01.790 --> 26:03.480
You have to burn a new outfit for me.

824
26:03.500 --> 26:05.120
I cannot go around looking like this.

825
26:05.150 --> 26:06.830
It's embarrassing!

826
26:06.980 --> 26:08.090
Why would you be embarrassed?

827
26:08.110 --> 26:09.190
I'm the only person who can see you.

828
26:09.210 --> 26:10.570
And you won't be embarrassed anymore,

829
26:10.590 --> 26:11.450
because I'm leaving.

830
26:11.460 --> 26:12.460
I'm going home!

831
26:12.990 --> 26:15.140
What about finding Gaysorn?

832
26:17.480 --> 26:18.550
The search for Grandma Gaysorn?

833
26:18.570 --> 26:19.310
Mm...

834
26:19.380 --> 26:21.110
Go ask the others for help, Grandpa.

835
26:21.130 --> 26:22.840
Because a burden like me,

836
26:22.860 --> 26:24.500
won't be able to help you.

837
26:25.310 --> 26:26.480
You are a grown man,

838
26:26.500 --> 26:27.950
but you still hold a grudge?!

839
26:28.120 --> 26:30.390
The burden I was talking about

840
26:30.410 --> 26:32.680
was your father!

841
26:32.700 --> 26:35.260
You assumed things on your own!

842
26:35.280 --> 26:36.320
Oh, wow...

843
26:36.720 --> 26:38.340
I went all in.

844
26:38.790 --> 26:40.010
Do you ever think that

845
26:40.030 --> 26:41.980
the reason Mom and Dad left

846
26:41.990 --> 26:43.910
was because you were stopping them from being happy?

847
26:46.100 --> 26:48.300
What would you know?!

848
26:48.320 --> 26:50.310
The reason I worked so hard

849
26:50.330 --> 26:53.150
to build this dorm,

850
26:53.170 --> 26:54.590
it was all for your mother,

851
26:54.610 --> 26:56.350
so she would be able to live comfortably!

852
26:56.370 --> 26:58.300
If she was truly happy,

853
26:58.490 --> 26:59.470
why did she run away?

854
27:01.800 --> 27:03.640
Well, your mother is stubborn!

855
27:04.020 --> 27:06.410
She did not want to live

856
27:06.430 --> 27:07.450
comfortably!

857
27:07.470 --> 27:10.680
Instead, she ran away to a hard life with your father in Nakhon Sawan!

858
27:11.400 --> 27:12.640
You wouldn't understand.

859
27:12.760 --> 27:14.150
Have you ever gone to check in on Mom

860
27:14.260 --> 27:15.880
after she ran away?!

861
27:15.890 --> 27:16.940
How could you know...?

862
27:19.000 --> 27:19.920
Ugh! Whatever.

863
27:19.940 --> 27:21.690
I'm going to sell this dorm.

864
27:21.710 --> 27:23.640
Mom and I don't want to keep it!

865
27:24.010 --> 27:25.010
Go ahead!

866
27:25.240 --> 27:26.630
If this dorm

867
27:27.090 --> 27:29.370
is such an eyesore for you,

868
27:29.400 --> 27:31.350
then sell it!

869
27:31.640 --> 27:32.550
And you...

870
27:32.820 --> 27:33.650
get out!

871
27:33.660 --> 27:35.150
Get out of here! Go!

872
27:35.170 --> 27:36.280
Yeah, I'll leave, alright!

873
27:36.370 --> 27:37.090
Go!

874
27:39.890 --> 27:42.380
Like mother, like son!

875
27:42.400 --> 27:45.600
How frustrating!

876
27:50.790 --> 27:52.570
Hello, Mom, I'm coming home today.

877
27:54.800 --> 27:55.600
Oh...

878
27:55.620 --> 27:57.880
I'm a bit sick of seeing some people at the dorm.

879
27:58.590 --> 28:00.990
To be honest, I miss your cooking too.

880
28:03.590 --> 28:05.900
I don't think there will be traffic. It'll probably take two hours.

881
28:08.590 --> 28:09.390
Mom,

882
28:09.780 --> 28:10.990
can I ask you something?

883
28:11.990 --> 28:13.630
Have you ever regretted

884
28:13.650 --> 28:15.020
running away to be with Dad?

885
28:16.710 --> 28:17.310
Huh?!

886
28:18.370 --> 28:20.110
You regret not taking Grandpa's money with you?

887
28:20.560 --> 28:21.230
Huh?

888
28:21.240 --> 28:22.580
Are you a scammer or something?

889
28:23.050 --> 28:24.690
Well...you're funny, Mom.

890
28:25.360 --> 28:26.600
Yeah, I'm on my way.

891
28:26.870 --> 28:27.780
Miss you.

892
28:27.790 --> 28:28.870
Muah, muah!

893
28:32.910 --> 28:33.910
Oh...

894
28:34.990 --> 28:35.990
Hey...

895
28:37.380 --> 28:38.380
Dollar,

896
28:38.550 --> 28:39.300
how did it go?

897
28:39.320 --> 28:40.560
Did you catch up with Din?

898
28:40.700 --> 28:42.240
Did you speak for Dome?

899
28:43.510 --> 28:44.510
Why are you crying?

900
28:44.530 --> 28:45.700
Did you fight?

901
28:45.720 --> 28:47.170
I pulled my eyelashes and it hurts.

902
28:47.190 --> 28:49.160
- Oh... - Oh...

903
28:50.190 --> 28:50.810
And...

904
28:50.820 --> 28:52.840
I don't know where Din went. We haven't talked.

905
28:53.090 --> 28:54.190
You don't have to talk to him.

906
28:54.910 --> 28:55.910
It won't change anything.

907
28:55.930 --> 28:57.160
In his eyes,

908
28:57.180 --> 28:58.530
I never grew up.

909
29:00.720 --> 29:02.200
I'm just a little brother...

910
29:02.690 --> 29:03.930
who can't think for myself.

911
29:03.950 --> 29:05.360
A brother who only causes trouble.

912
29:07.900 --> 29:08.800
Dominiga,

913
29:09.010 --> 29:10.330
don't be sad.

914
29:10.350 --> 29:11.910
No matter what people say,

915
29:11.930 --> 29:14.590
I'll always be by your side.

916
29:15.900 --> 29:17.770
Just like what NewJiew said,

917
29:18.280 --> 29:20.400
"If you don't love me, don't act nice or act like you care."

918
29:20.510 --> 29:22.640
"If you don't love me, don't try to protect or order me around."

919
29:22.660 --> 29:24.640
- "'Cause my heart is fragile." - "'Cause my heart is fragile."

920
29:25.590 --> 29:27.070
- Wow... - That was perfect.

921
29:27.090 --> 29:28.380
You did that perfectly, dear.

922
29:29.290 --> 29:30.250
You were dancing, does it mean

923
29:30.260 --> 29:32.220
that you're not mad at Din anymore?

924
29:33.970 --> 29:36.280
I wasn't that mad at Din,

925
29:36.670 --> 29:38.600
but my family is like this.

926
29:38.750 --> 29:40.150
They put limitations on me ever since I was young.

927
29:40.170 --> 29:41.880
Whether it's what I study or what I do...

928
29:42.280 --> 29:44.380
They never asked if I'm fine with those things.

929
29:44.390 --> 29:46.230
Ugh...

930
29:46.250 --> 29:47.690
Dollar is like that too!

931
29:48.710 --> 29:49.740
Back then,

932
29:49.760 --> 29:52.470
he tried to force me into the Police Cadet Academy.

933
29:53.680 --> 29:55.030
But I didn't listen.

934
29:55.050 --> 29:57.710
When he couldn't force me mentally,

935
29:57.740 --> 30:00.040
he forced me

936
30:00.060 --> 30:01.630
to exercise physically instead!

937
30:01.670 --> 30:03.310
- Look. - Ooh, mm...

938
30:03.580 --> 30:04.810
- Ugh... - It's solid.

939
30:04.830 --> 30:06.550
I was worried about you back then,

940
30:06.570 --> 30:08.370
because the fashion major you wanted to get into

941
30:08.390 --> 30:10.160
didn't look like it could provide for you.

942
30:10.180 --> 30:11.800
You must think about your future, too.

943
30:11.820 --> 30:13.300
If I wasn't here with you,

944
30:13.320 --> 30:14.710
how will you and Mom live?

945
30:14.720 --> 30:16.100
Your words are wise,

946
30:16.950 --> 30:18.830
but your eyelashes are so extra.

947
30:19.950 --> 30:21.550
Let me take them off for you.

948
30:21.860 --> 30:22.790
I'll pull them off.

949
30:22.810 --> 30:24.830
Leave my eyelashes alone!

950
30:24.850 --> 30:26.180
Hey...

951
30:26.610 --> 30:27.870
Hey, Dome,

952
30:28.060 --> 30:29.060
I think Din

953
30:29.470 --> 30:30.920
didn't want to cut ties with you.

954
30:32.110 --> 30:33.110
The reason he did that

955
30:33.130 --> 30:34.690
was because he was worried.

956
30:35.330 --> 30:36.550
Just like how I'm

957
30:36.570 --> 30:37.910
worried about Dolly.

958
30:40.610 --> 30:42.220
I understand,

959
30:42.590 --> 30:44.010
but I don't think it's fair

960
30:44.600 --> 30:45.890
Din got to become a police.

961
30:46.130 --> 30:47.470
He gets to do what he loves.

962
30:48.710 --> 30:49.810
What about me?

963
30:50.010 --> 30:52.000
Can't I do something I love as well?

964
30:58.180 --> 30:59.760
Then are you sure

965
30:59.780 --> 31:02.160
that the job you love

966
31:02.190 --> 31:03.910
can actually sustain you?

967
31:05.150 --> 31:06.520
Hey, Dominiga,

968
31:06.980 --> 31:08.300
tell him.

969
31:08.320 --> 31:11.370
Say it with confidence.

970
31:12.930 --> 31:13.560
No.

971
31:16.230 --> 31:18.230
- I lost my footing... - I'm just saying that

972
31:18.250 --> 31:19.840
I'll try my best.

973
31:19.990 --> 31:21.620
Because in his eyes,

974
31:21.640 --> 31:23.800
working as a drag queen

975
31:23.820 --> 31:25.010
is an unstable job.

976
31:25.390 --> 31:27.190
But wouldn't it be better

977
31:27.240 --> 31:30.200
if I get to do what I truly enjoy?

978
31:33.190 --> 31:34.790
Your younger brother said it.

979
31:35.690 --> 31:36.830
What do you think, big brother?

980
31:36.850 --> 31:38.000
- Huh? - Huh?

981
31:45.210 --> 31:46.600
But what if...

982
31:47.260 --> 31:49.090
it doesn't work out?

983
31:50.000 --> 31:51.530
What will you do with your life?

984
31:58.090 --> 32:00.200
I'll have to find a new job, Din.

985
32:00.840 --> 32:02.230
But not a police.

986
32:05.450 --> 32:06.590
To be honest,

987
32:07.590 --> 32:09.010
there is no job

988
32:09.290 --> 32:10.510
that's a hundred percent stable.

989
32:10.900 --> 32:12.030
It depends...

990
32:12.330 --> 32:14.190
on how you live your life.

991
32:15.190 --> 32:18.220
Din, please give me a chance.

992
32:28.200 --> 32:29.740
Then we should head home, have a meal,

993
32:31.730 --> 32:32.930
and talk to our parents about this.

994
32:34.350 --> 32:35.680
If they disagree,

995
32:36.790 --> 32:38.110
I'll try to talk to them.

996
32:38.820 --> 32:39.860
Really?!

997
32:43.230 --> 32:45.040
- Let's go, then! - Hey, wait.

998
32:45.060 --> 32:46.130
You should get changed,

999
32:46.150 --> 32:47.800
- or our parents might have a heart attack. - Get changed?

1000
32:47.820 --> 32:48.700
Okay.

1001
32:48.720 --> 32:50.590
- Change your outfit. - Change, change.

1002
32:50.650 --> 32:51.280
Get changed.

1003
32:52.060 --> 32:52.900
Thank you, Din,

1004
32:52.920 --> 32:53.720
for listening to Dome.

1005
32:53.740 --> 32:54.780
Ugh!

1006
32:55.170 --> 32:56.070
Can I ask you one thing?

1007
32:56.230 --> 32:57.230
Will you remove your eyelashes?

1008
32:57.670 --> 32:58.990
It's annoying to look at.

1009
32:59.010 --> 32:59.770
You don't like it?

1010
32:59.790 --> 33:00.690
No, I don't!

1011
33:00.710 --> 33:01.620
- Stop! - You don't like it?

1012
33:01.640 --> 33:02.510
Go take them off.

1013
33:03.430 --> 33:04.100
But it's pretty.

1014
33:04.130 --> 33:05.000
Hey, take your friend away.

1015
33:05.030 --> 33:06.520
Hello, this is Daisy.

1016
33:09.420 --> 33:10.880
I was...practicing my script earlier.

1017
33:10.990 --> 33:11.590
Huh?!

1018
33:12.400 --> 33:13.680
You can't contact Dobby?

1019
33:16.000 --> 33:17.000
Dobby.

1020
33:18.120 --> 33:18.800
Dobby.

1021
33:19.070 --> 33:19.960
Are you here?

1022
33:20.600 --> 33:23.590
Oh, why am I hiding? He cannot see me anyway.

1023
33:23.680 --> 33:24.340
Dobby.

1024
33:27.300 --> 33:28.180
Dobby!

1025
33:32.680 --> 33:33.680
His bag isn't here as well.

1026
33:34.290 --> 33:36.720
How could it be here? He already went to Nakhon Sawan.

1027
33:37.090 --> 33:37.990
Dobby...

1028
33:39.030 --> 33:40.580
But his car is still here.

1029
33:43.190 --> 33:43.860
Gramps.

1030
33:44.390 --> 33:45.860
Gramps, Gramps.

1031
33:46.010 --> 33:47.430
If you can hear me,

1032
33:47.610 --> 33:48.990
please help me look for Dobby.

1033
33:49.240 --> 33:50.710
His mother is very worried.

1034
33:52.290 --> 33:53.870
Please tell him to call his mother back.

1035
33:54.000 --> 33:54.880
Thank you.

1036
33:55.490 --> 33:56.490
Thank you, Gramps.

1037
33:58.410 --> 34:00.210
What does this have to do with me?!

1038
34:00.980 --> 34:03.890
It is not my duty to look for him!

1039
34:09.300 --> 34:10.690
Maybe I should look for him...

1040
34:11.290 --> 34:12.600
So that he...

1041
34:13.190 --> 34:14.510
burns me a new outfit.

1042
34:20.010 --> 34:21.280
Dobby!

1043
34:21.810 --> 34:22.830
Dobby!

1044
34:24.010 --> 34:24.940
Dobby?

1045
34:24.969 --> 34:26.909
Dobby, where are you?

1046
34:26.929 --> 34:28.060
Dobby!

1047
34:29.040 --> 34:30.440
Dobby!

1048
34:30.460 --> 34:31.510
Dobby!

1049
34:33.199 --> 34:37.699
Dobby!

1050
34:38.699 --> 34:39.920
Dobby!

1051
34:39.940 --> 34:43.080
Hey, do you still exist? I can't find you anywhere!

1052
34:43.100 --> 34:44.100
Dobby!

1053
34:45.610 --> 34:46.670
Dobby!

1054
34:46.690 --> 34:49.100
Dobby, where are...

1055
34:49.120 --> 34:49.679
Oh?

1056
34:50.130 --> 34:51.310
The manhole cover is open.

1057
34:51.330 --> 34:53.350
Oh...that's dangerous.

1058
34:53.370 --> 34:55.760
Someone might fall in there.

1059
34:55.780 --> 34:57.830
It's probably Daeng the Handyman's fault.

1060
34:58.460 --> 35:00.950
Oh, this is...

1061
35:01.290 --> 35:01.840
Huh?!

1062
35:04.090 --> 35:05.000
Dobby.

1063
35:05.090 --> 35:06.810
Help, please help Dobby!

1064
35:06.830 --> 35:08.140
Hold on, alright?

1065
35:08.160 --> 35:09.720
I will find someone to help you.

1066
35:09.740 --> 35:10.970
Anybody!

1067
35:10.990 --> 35:11.760
Help!

1068
35:11.790 --> 35:13.420
Dobby fell down the sewer!

1069
35:13.440 --> 35:16.510
Dobby!!

1070
35:19.910 --> 35:20.920
Ugh...

1071
35:26.800 --> 35:27.930
why do you have to keep this up?

1072
35:27.950 --> 35:30.300
Just say you'll make up and be friends,

1073
35:30.320 --> 35:31.870
and we'll let you go to the toilet.

1074
35:32.180 --> 35:32.940
Yes.

1075
35:33.190 --> 35:35.370
I don't mind doing that.

1076
35:35.590 --> 35:36.870
I can make up with him,

1077
35:38.300 --> 35:39.410
but he has to apologize first!

1078
35:39.440 --> 35:40.310
Oh...

1079
35:40.560 --> 35:42.490
Never...

1080
35:43.160 --> 35:43.950
Oh...

1081
35:45.920 --> 35:46.920
Ow...

1082
35:47.430 --> 35:48.800
I think we should let them go.

1083
35:48.820 --> 35:50.010
If they pee themselves here,

1084
35:50.030 --> 35:50.690
who will clean it up?

1085
35:50.710 --> 35:51.370
No.

1086
35:51.990 --> 35:53.470
They'll have to clean it on their own.

1087
35:54.920 --> 35:56.370
Think about

1088
35:56.390 --> 35:57.640
what you're going to do next.

1089
35:57.660 --> 35:58.660
Since I'm

1090
35:58.680 --> 35:59.760
not in a rush anyway.

1091
36:01.910 --> 36:03.100
I'll turn on the music while I wait.

1092
36:04.510 --> 36:08.520
♫Let it flow out♫

1093
36:25.350 --> 36:25.970
Everyone!

1094
36:25.990 --> 36:27.190
- Huh? - Everyone, everyone!

1095
36:27.210 --> 36:27.920
Whoa...

1096
36:28.190 --> 36:29.640
Has anyone seen Mr. Dobby?

1097
36:29.660 --> 36:30.760
What's wrong, Guard Dum?

1098
36:30.890 --> 36:32.150
Mr. Dobby went missing.

1099
36:32.170 --> 36:33.180
- Huh?! - Huh?!

1100
36:33.510 --> 36:36.630
Mr. Dax, Mr. Dolly, and Mr. Dollar were searching. No one could contact him!

1101
36:36.650 --> 36:38.660
- Everyone, let's go find Dobby! - Whoa....

1102
36:38.680 --> 36:40.000
- Ow, ow, ow. - Guard Dum, go!

1103
36:40.020 --> 36:41.470
- Lead the way, Guard Dum. - Where is he?!

1104
36:41.490 --> 36:42.630
- Quickly! - Guard Dum, go!

1105
36:42.660 --> 36:44.840
Don't leave yet. Let me go...

1106
36:44.860 --> 36:46.120
Ugh, stop shouting.

1107
36:46.140 --> 36:46.950
The key is right there.

1108
36:49.300 --> 36:50.910
It's so far away,

1109
36:50.930 --> 36:51.860
I can't reach it!

1110
36:51.910 --> 36:53.220
We can, we have to.

1111
36:53.740 --> 36:54.520
Oh!

1112
36:55.130 --> 36:56.610
Put your arm here.

1113
36:59.910 --> 37:00.800
Ow...

1114
37:04.300 --> 37:04.930
Hey!

1115
37:06.560 --> 37:07.560
Whoa!

1116
37:24.750 --> 37:26.610
Duang! [Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

1117
37:26.630 --> 37:27.300
Danis!

1118
37:27.320 --> 37:28.580
Where did they all go?

1119
37:28.600 --> 37:30.830
Come help Dobby!

1120
37:30.850 --> 37:33.100
How can I help him? I can't!

1121
37:40.130 --> 37:41.520
- Gramps?! - Gramps?!

1122
37:44.130 --> 37:45.040
You can see me?

1123
37:46.590 --> 37:49.750
Go help Dobby! He fell down the sewer!

1124
37:50.670 --> 37:54.480
A ghost!

1125
38:00.330 --> 38:01.580
Was that real?

1126
38:02.090 --> 38:03.090
What the heck?!

1127
38:03.600 --> 38:04.600
Gramps!

1128
38:05.000 --> 38:10.320
[The D Dorm]

1129
38:11.890 --> 38:12.890
Here's your medicine.

1130
38:14.430 --> 38:15.850
- Ow... - Thanks a lot.

1131
38:15.880 --> 38:16.880
Whoa.

1132
38:18.510 --> 38:20.170
- It stings... - Are you really alright?

1133
38:23.100 --> 38:23.600
Whoa.

1134
38:24.010 --> 38:25.670
You got a head injury.

1135
38:25.690 --> 38:26.710
Is your brain still working?

1136
38:26.850 --> 38:27.910
Do you remember who I am?

1137
38:30.670 --> 38:31.990
Would you like me to call you Dax or Daisy, then?

1138
38:32.010 --> 38:32.780
Oh,

1139
38:32.800 --> 38:34.290
you can call me Daisy.

1140
38:34.310 --> 38:36.840
- Come here, let me give you a smooch. - Hey!

1141
38:36.860 --> 38:37.860
Dax, stop!

1142
38:37.890 --> 38:39.490
Don't, don't, don't, Dax!

1143
38:40.440 --> 38:41.550
- Dax, don't tease me! Ow! - Whoa!

1144
38:41.790 --> 38:43.150
- Dax, stop. It hurts! - Whoa!

1145
38:43.170 --> 38:46.420
Am I interrupting something? I can come back later.

1146
38:46.440 --> 38:47.280
Hey!

1147
38:47.300 --> 38:48.140
Hey, hey, hey, wait!

1148
38:48.160 --> 38:49.630
- Get off me, Dax! - What?

1149
38:49.650 --> 38:50.950
- What is it? - Don't play along.

1150
38:50.980 --> 38:51.640
Oh, okay.

1151
38:51.660 --> 38:52.590
What do you need?

1152
38:52.610 --> 38:54.480
I brought you a first-aid kit.

1153
38:54.500 --> 38:56.960
So after you take a shower, you can change your bandage.

1154
38:56.980 --> 38:58.110
Oh, you may continue.

1155
38:58.130 --> 38:59.900
- Huh? Don't go yet. - Wait, wait.

1156
38:59.920 --> 39:01.200
By the way,

1157
39:01.220 --> 39:03.190
I told Daeng the Handyman to close the manhole cover.

1158
39:03.610 --> 39:05.800
Don't be mad at him, alright?

1159
39:05.820 --> 39:07.880
He didn't mean to be careless.

1160
39:07.900 --> 39:08.900
Just...

1161
39:09.390 --> 39:10.790
Some stuff happened...

1162
39:11.100 --> 39:13.040
Thank you for saving me.

1163
39:13.890 --> 39:15.240
No need to thank me.

1164
39:15.260 --> 39:16.260
You should thank Gramps.

1165
39:16.560 --> 39:17.990
- Huh? - Mm.

1166
39:20.120 --> 39:21.590
Dawin told me

1167
39:21.610 --> 39:23.720
Gramps suddenly showed up

1168
39:23.740 --> 39:25.090
to tell him that you...

1169
39:25.110 --> 39:26.950
fell down the sewer. And sent him to help you.

1170
39:26.970 --> 39:27.670
Huh?!

1171
39:27.690 --> 39:28.900
Dawin saw Grandpa?

1172
39:28.930 --> 39:29.930
That's what he told me.

1173
39:29.950 --> 39:31.140
Don't believe him too much.

1174
39:31.340 --> 39:33.490
He was probably delirious from holding in his pee.

1175
39:33.510 --> 39:34.320
- I see... - Well...

1176
39:34.420 --> 39:35.810
What did he say again?

1177
39:35.830 --> 39:38.510
Gramps was wearing drag then he...hey!

1178
39:38.530 --> 39:39.410
- Dobby! - You...

1179
39:39.430 --> 39:39.940
What's wrong, Dobby?

1180
39:39.970 --> 39:41.220
Hey, are you alright?

1181
39:41.240 --> 39:42.990
- Dobby, did you choke? - I'm fine.

1182
39:43.010 --> 39:43.870
- I'm fine, Ms. Danis. - Dobby...

1183
39:43.900 --> 39:45.070
But I'm not fine because of you.

1184
39:45.090 --> 39:45.680
What?

1185
39:45.700 --> 39:47.460
- Was it too soft? - Oh, it's too harsh.

1186
39:47.960 --> 39:49.310
- Hit me gently. It hurts. - Ugh.

1187
39:49.330 --> 39:51.970
Take care of yourself, then. I'm tired of you guys.

1188
39:52.690 --> 39:53.270
Hey.

1189
39:53.480 --> 39:55.590
Stop hitting me and go look for something to help me.

1190
39:55.620 --> 39:56.690
Aw, aren't we going to continue?

1191
39:56.710 --> 39:58.180
That's enough!

1192
39:58.200 --> 39:59.470
Here, I'll dress your wound.

1193
40:02.880 --> 40:03.950
We don't have any Mia cloth.

1194
40:04.220 --> 40:04.970
What? Mia cloth?

1195
40:04.990 --> 40:05.630
Goth.

1196
40:05.660 --> 40:06.660
Wow...

1197
40:07.000 --> 40:07.740
Ow...

1198
40:07.760 --> 40:08.270
- It hurts even worse. - Oh...

1199
40:08.290 --> 40:09.510
Did you laugh to the point that it hurt?

1200
40:09.530 --> 40:10.530
It's your joke that hurts.

1201
40:11.180 --> 40:12.120
- Let me look around. - Quickly.

1202
40:12.140 --> 40:13.910
Just find one.

1203
40:19.780 --> 40:20.780
Whoa...

1204
40:22.290 --> 40:23.700
It's a big wound, too.

1205
40:24.580 --> 40:25.890
Is this your house?

1206
40:27.000 --> 40:27.850
Here.

1207
40:31.440 --> 40:33.720
- Whoa. - Is this kid you?

1208
41:11.700 --> 41:13.800
Dobby, are you hurt?

1209
41:14.330 --> 41:15.110
I am hurt.

1210
41:15.410 --> 41:16.080
Huh?

1211
41:16.300 --> 41:17.530
I fell down a sewer, you know?

1212
41:18.290 --> 41:19.450
You were not asleep?

1213
41:22.080 --> 41:23.510
I couldn't fall asleep, Grandpa.

1214
41:25.200 --> 41:26.540
I want to ask you something.

1215
41:26.810 --> 41:27.810
What?

1216
41:28.990 --> 41:31.190
Ever since Mom went to live with Dad,

1217
41:31.600 --> 41:33.360
have you ever gone to check in on her?

1218
41:47.440 --> 41:49.180
Why did you go find her, Grandpa?

1219
41:49.790 --> 41:51.640
Didn't you already cut ties with her?

1220
41:56.050 --> 41:57.310
I just wanted to see

1221
41:57.330 --> 42:01.520
the state of her after she left to be with your father.

1222
42:04.400 --> 42:05.710
You missed my mom, didn't you?

1223
42:13.810 --> 42:16.180
That is none of your business.

1224
42:16.200 --> 42:17.350
What about you?

1225
42:17.370 --> 42:19.090
You said you would go back to Nakhon Sawan

1226
42:19.110 --> 42:21.950
to that little rat hole house of yours, did you not?

1227
42:22.820 --> 42:24.020
How can I go back, Grandpa?

1228
42:24.040 --> 42:25.600
Look at me.

1229
42:25.620 --> 42:26.580
Look.

1230
42:26.600 --> 42:27.600
Look!

1231
42:28.500 --> 42:31.000
If I went back looking like this,

1232
42:31.550 --> 42:32.550
your dorm

1233
42:32.680 --> 42:34.560
would be destroyed.

1234
42:35.450 --> 42:36.180
Oh...

1235
42:36.470 --> 42:39.390
Take some rest, then.

1236
42:40.880 --> 42:42.790
I do not want you to perish.

1237
42:42.820 --> 42:44.770
Because if you did,

1238
42:44.790 --> 42:48.240
there will be two ghosts in the same den.

1239
42:51.090 --> 42:53.110
You do not have to thank me.

1240
42:53.130 --> 42:54.680
Just...

1241
42:54.700 --> 42:56.510
burn me a new outfit.

1242
42:56.530 --> 42:57.920
That would be enough.

1243
42:57.940 --> 43:00.430
Because each time I look at this outfit,

1244
43:00.450 --> 43:03.000
it reminds me of a movie. I cannot recall the name...

1245
43:03.020 --> 43:06.200
The director is called Poj Arnon.

1246
43:06.220 --> 43:07.600
He made a lot of movies.

1247
43:07.620 --> 43:09.060
There is this one scene

1248
43:09.080 --> 43:11.590
in which a character said,

1249
43:11.610 --> 43:13.150
"Who killed Araya"?

1250
43:13.170 --> 43:14.310
And another person answered,

1251
43:14.600 --> 43:15.710
"Payoon..."

1252
43:15.890 --> 43:16.930
Then she went quiet.

1253
43:16.960 --> 43:18.100
And suddenly, she said,

1254
43:18.210 --> 43:19.110
"is not the killer!"

1255
43:19.130 --> 43:20.410
So the other person replied,

1256
43:20.640 --> 43:22.390
"You timed that so horribly"!

1257
43:23.110 --> 43:24.500
Oh, it made me laugh.

1258
43:24.530 --> 43:25.560
I really liked that one.

1259
43:25.580 --> 43:27.600
- Ow, ow... - It is stuck in my head.

1260
43:28.360 --> 43:29.190
- You... - Go watch it.

1261
43:29.210 --> 43:30.070
You don't remember the name,

1262
43:30.090 --> 43:31.130
- but you remember all the dialogues? - Yeah.

1263
43:31.150 --> 43:32.550
But I really enjoyed it.

1264
43:32.570 --> 43:33.130
- You did? - Yeah.

1265
43:33.150 --> 43:34.510
- Yeah. - I'll go watch it.

1266
43:34.540 --> 43:35.430
I liked it.

1267
43:35.450 --> 43:37.380
Go argue with yourself outside, Grandpa.

1268
43:37.410 --> 43:38.950
Oh, rest up.

1269
43:38.980 --> 43:40.680
But you have to watch it.

1270
43:40.700 --> 43:42.010
- Yeah, I got it. - Good.

1271
43:44.200 --> 43:49.500
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

1272
43:50.840 --> 43:51.640
Call out to him.

1273
43:51.660 --> 43:53.060
Hey!

1274
43:54.160 --> 43:54.690
Ugh.

1275
43:54.710 --> 43:56.050
Stop making loud noises.

1276
43:56.070 --> 43:57.760
It's disturbing other tenants!

1277
43:58.390 --> 44:00.330
Who told you about us?

1278
44:00.440 --> 44:01.440
I did.

1279
44:01.630 --> 44:02.490
Kappa?

1280
44:02.880 --> 44:04.450
- Would you like this, then?! - Whoa, whoa, whoa.

1281
44:04.470 --> 44:05.880
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

1282
44:05.900 --> 44:06.760
Dawin!

1283
44:06.780 --> 44:08.380
Why do you want to see Gramps' ghost again?

1284
44:08.400 --> 44:10.660
I just want to prove

1285
44:10.700 --> 44:12.180
if I have the ability to see ghosts.

1286
44:12.200 --> 44:13.210
I tried it all.

1287
44:13.230 --> 44:14.620
From looking between my legs

1288
44:14.640 --> 44:16.290
to wearing dead people's clothes.

1289
44:16.310 --> 44:17.950
But there's one method I haven't tried yet.

1290
44:18.230 --> 44:19.310
Would you like to try it out tonight?

